<title>USA: US banks free reserves $965 mln/day two weeks ended June 4.</title>
<headline>US banks free reserves $965 mln/day two weeks ended June 4.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. commercial banks had free reserves of $965 million per day in the two weeks ended June 4, versus revised free reserves of $883 million in the previous two-week period, the Federal Reserve said.</p>
<p>Seasonal borrowings were $210 million versus $169 million a day. Extended credits were nil.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
